{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"type CursorExpressions = object;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/types.ts#L298","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/db/src/types.ts:298"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cursor expressions for pagination, passed separately from the main "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"where"},{"type":"text","value":" clause.\nThe sync layer can choose to use cursor-based pagination (combining these with the where)\nor offset-based pagination (ignoring these and using the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"offset"},{"type":"text","value":" parameter)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Neither expression includes the main "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"where"},{"type":"text","value":" clause - they are cursor-specific only."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"properties","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Properties"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"lastkey","children":[{"type":"text","value":"lastKey?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional lastKey: string | number;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/types.ts#L316","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/db/src/types.ts:316"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The key of the last item that was loaded.\nCan be used by sync layers for tracking or deduplication."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"wherecurrent","children":[{"type":"text","value":"whereCurrent"}]},{"type":"code","value":"whereCurrent: BasicExpression<boolean>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/types.ts#L311","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/db/src/types.ts:311"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Expression for rows equal to the current cursor value (first orderBy column only).\nUsed to handle tie-breaking/duplicates at the boundary.\nExample: eq(col1, v1) or for Dates: and(gte(col1, v1), lt(col1, v1+1ms))"}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"wherefrom","children":[{"type":"text","value":"whereFrom"}]},{"type":"code","value":"whereFrom: BasicExpression<boolean>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/types.ts#L305","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/db/src/types.ts:305"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Expression for rows greater than (after) the cursor value.\nCore emits this predicate from the leading order column. Multi-column\nqueries load the complete leading-value tie separately instead of\nconstructing a composite cursor."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"properties","text":"Properties","level":2},{"id":"lastkey","text":"lastKey?","level":3},{"id":"wherecurrent","text":"whereCurrent","level":3},{"id":"wherefrom","text":"whereFrom","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\ntype CursorExpressions = object;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/db/src/types.ts:298](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/types.ts#L298)\n\nCursor expressions for pagination, passed separately from the main `where` clause.\nThe sync layer can choose to use cursor-based pagination (combining these with the where)\nor offset-based pagination (ignoring these and using the `offset` parameter).\n\nNeither expression includes the main `where` clause - they are cursor-specific only.\n\n## Properties\n\n### lastKey?\n\n```ts\noptional lastKey: string | number;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/db/src/types.ts:316](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/types.ts#L316)\n\nThe key of the last item that was loaded.\nCan be used by sync layers for tracking or deduplication.\n\n***\n\n### whereCurrent\n\n```ts\nwhereCurrent: BasicExpression<boolean>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/db/src/types.ts:311](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/types.ts#L311)\n\nExpression for rows equal to the current cursor value (first orderBy column only).\nUsed to handle tie-breaking/duplicates at the boundary.\nExample: eq(col1, v1) or for Dates: and(gte(col1, v1), lt(col1, v1+1ms))\n\n***\n\n### whereFrom\n\n```ts\nwhereFrom: BasicExpression<boolean>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/db/src/types.ts:305](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/types.ts#L305)\n\nExpression for rows greater than (after) the cursor value.\nCore emits this predicate from the leading order column. Multi-column\nqueries load the complete leading-value tie separately instead of\nconstructing a composite cursor.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: CursorExpressions\ntitle: CursorExpressions\n---\n\n```ts\ntype CursorExpressions = object;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/db/src/types.ts:298](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/types.ts#L298)\n\nCursor expressions for pagination, passed separately from the main `where` clause.\nThe sync layer can choose to use cursor-based pagination (combining these with the where)\nor offset-based pagination (ignoring these and using the `offset` parameter).\n\nNeither expression includes the main `where` clause - they are cursor-specific only.\n\n## Properties\n\n### lastKey?\n\n```ts\noptional lastKey: string | number;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/db/src/types.ts:316](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/types.ts#L316)\n\nThe key of the last item that was loaded.\nCan be used by sync layers for tracking or deduplication.\n\n***\n\n### whereCurrent\n\n```ts\nwhereCurrent: BasicExpression<boolean>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/db/src/types.ts:311](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/types.ts#L311)\n\nExpression for rows equal to the current cursor value (first orderBy column only).\nUsed to handle tie-breaking/duplicates at the boundary.\nExample: eq(col1, v1) or for Dates: and(gte(col1, v1), lt(col1, v1+1ms))\n\n***\n\n### whereFrom\n\n```ts\nwhereFrom: BasicExpression<boolean>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/db/src/types.ts:305](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/types.ts#L305)\n\nExpression for rows greater than (after) the cursor value.\nCore emits this predicate from the leading order column. Multi-column\nqueries load the complete leading-value tie separately instead of\nconstructing a composite cursor.\n"}
